<article class="env-remark" id="0GFC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GFC">Remark <span data-tag="0GFC">75.16.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space over $S$. Let $G$ be a perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ which is a generator for $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. By Theorem <a href="/tag/09IY" data-tag="09IY">75.15.4</a> there is at least one of these. Combining Lemma <a href="/tag/08F3" data-tag="08F3">75.5.3</a> with Proposition <a href="/tag/09M8" data-tag="09M8">75.16.1</a> and with Derived Categories, Proposition <a href="/tag/09SR" data-tag="09SR">13.37.6</a> we see that $G$ is a classical generator for $D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article>